\r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_-4366781377798804178_m_7114722397003852669_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0px 5px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/t/4f490fbadc7ca28a?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/t/4f490fbadc7ca28a?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366368383000&amp;usg=AOvVaw27beWvGhh023a66vDJZ_6z\">\r\n      display of ECDF\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tbody><tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          Kavee L &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">xcub...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Dec 17 11:04AM -0800\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Hi Bogdan,<br>\r\n <br>\r\nWhat do you mean by &quot;Equal distance&quot;? In your example, those break points <br>\r\nare not uniformly distributed (neither in original form or after log <br>\r\ntransformed). <br>\r\nFor example 0.1 is 10-fold smaller than 1, but the next break, &quot;5&quot;, is <br>\r\n5-fold bigger than 1. Do you want these two number to be represent in the <br>\r\nx-axis with equally distance from &quot;1&quot;?<br>\r\nMy guess is if you can define a function to transform those breaks back <br>\r\ninto a linear scale, you should be able to use that to transform your data <br>\r\nand plot them.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nBest,<br>\r\nKavee<br>\r\n <br>\r\nOn Monday, December 17, 2018 at 4:43:00 AM UTC-5, Bogdan Tanasa wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_-4366781377798804178_m_7114722397003852669_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:rgb(245,245,245);padding:5px 20px\">\r\n  <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n  <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding-top:4px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(99,99,99);font-size:11px\">\r\n      \r\n      You received this digest because you&#39;re subscribed to updates for this group. You can change your settings on the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/ggplot2/join\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/ggplot2/join&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366368383000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2AmNAP8SiHDt8pMC96rl4t\">group membership page</a>.<br>\r\n      To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr></tbody>\r\n  </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
